description:
Build a trie of lowercase words, and the Knuth-Morris-Pratt search:

```cpp
class Trie
{
public:
    bool insert(const std::string& word);       // false if already present; words are lowercase a-z, possibly empty
    bool erase(const std::string& word);        // false if absent
    bool contains(const std::string& word) const;
    int countPrefix(const std::string& prefix) const;   // how many stored words start with it
    std::vector<std::string> complete(const std::string& prefix, std::size_t limit) const;   // alphabetical
    std::string longestCommonPrefix() const;    // of all stored words; "" if none
    std::size_t size() const;
};

std::vector<int> prefixFunction(const std::string& p);
std::vector<std::size_t> findAll(const std::string& text, const std::string& pattern);   // overlapping matches; {} for an empty pattern
```

- Each node keeps how many words pass through it, so `countPrefix` is O(length of the prefix). `erase` decreases those counts and must leave the trie consistent (the tests insert again afterwards).
- `complete` returns up to `limit` stored words that start with `prefix`, in alphabetical order (depth-first, children in letter order), including the prefix itself if it is a word.
- `findAll` must be O(n + m): the tests search a million characters.

